WEBVTT

00:00:00.015 --> 00:00:02.736
Easy Folk Tales. The Ugly Duckling.

00:00:02.736 --> 00:00:05.469
One summer a mother duck sat on her eggs.

00:00:05.469 --> 00:00:09.752
One by one the eggs opened, and little yellow ducklings came out.

00:00:09.752 --> 00:00:12.305
But the last egg was bigger than the others.

00:00:12.305 --> 00:00:15.259
When it opened, out came a large gray bird.

00:00:15.259 --> 00:00:18.050
"What an ugly duckling," said the other ducks.

00:00:18.050 --> 00:00:19.778
They bit him and pushed him.

00:00:19.778 --> 00:00:22.405
Even his brothers and sisters laughed at him.

00:00:22.405 --> 00:00:24.209
Every day it got worse.

00:00:24.209 --> 00:00:26.733
At last the ugly duckling ran away.

00:00:26.733 --> 00:00:28.566
He lived alone by a lake.

00:00:28.566 --> 00:00:33.175
In the autumn he saw some beautiful white birds flying high over his head.

00:00:33.175 --> 00:00:35.613
They had long necks and wide wings.

00:00:35.613 --> 00:00:40.631
He did not know what they were, but he loved them more than anything he had ever seen.

00:00:40.631 --> 00:00:42.997
The winter was long and very cold.

00:00:42.997 --> 00:00:46.364
The water turned to ice, and the duckling almost died.

00:00:46.364 --> 00:00:48.323
But at last the spring came.

00:00:48.323 --> 00:00:50.087
The sun was warm again.

00:00:50.087 --> 00:00:54.180
The duckling opened his wings, and they were stronger than before.

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:57.441
He flew up and came down on a lake in a garden.

00:00:57.441 --> 00:01:00.347
Three of the beautiful white birds were swimming there.

00:01:00.347 --> 00:01:03.842
"They will kill me because I am so ugly," he thought.

00:01:03.842 --> 00:01:05.386
"But I do not care.

00:01:05.386 --> 00:01:06.914
I want to be near them."

00:01:06.914 --> 00:01:09.487
He swam toward them and put his head down.

00:01:09.487 --> 00:01:12.006
Then he saw himself in the clear water.

00:01:12.006 --> 00:01:15.075
He was not a gray, ugly bird any longer.

00:01:15.075 --> 00:01:16.278
He was a swan.

00:01:16.278 --> 00:01:19.575
The other swans swam around him and touched him gently.

00:01:19.575 --> 00:01:21.714
Some children ran into the garden.

00:01:21.714 --> 00:01:24.555
"Look, there is a new one!" they shouted.

00:01:24.555 --> 00:01:26.778
"And he is the most beautiful of all."

00:01:26.778 --> 00:01:29.444
The young swan hid his head under his wing.

00:01:29.444 --> 00:01:32.624
He was so happy that he did not know what to do.

00:01:32.624 --> 00:01:35.183
He remembered how everyone had laughed at him.

00:01:35.183 --> 00:01:38.736
And now they said he was the most beautiful bird of all.
